  "facts": [
    "The new Governor Mario M. Cuomo Bridge opened its north span to westbound traffic on August 26, 2017, and the south span followed just a month later, completing the first fully operational twin cable‑stayed bridge in the U.S. in 2018.",
    "Construction relied on the Left Coast Lifter, one of the world’s largest cranes, to lift pre‑assembled girders one full span at a time, a feat that required precise coordination and massive lifting capacity.",
    "During construction, a crane collapse on July 19, 2016, sent a heavy piece onto the old bridge, injuring five people but sparing lives, a rare incident that highlighted the project’s high‑stakes environment."
  ],
